# ebaybiz — gitignore
#
# THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC. It holds the pipeline (prompts, lib, templates,
# tests) and nothing else. Three classes of file must never reach it:
#
#   1. SECRETS      — API tokens and credentials.
#   2. BUSINESS DATA — what we own, what we asked, what we were paid. Revenue,
#                      sale prices, ledgers, and the reports built from them.
#   3. HEAVY/GENERATED — shoot photos, similarity indexes, per-run phase output.
#                      Regenerable, large, and specific to one operator's stock.
#
# When adding a rule, say which class it belongs to. When in doubt about a file
# that contains numbers from real sales: it is business data, exclude it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 1. SECRETS
# Live config holds API tokens — never commit. Use lib/config.example.yaml
# as the template for new setups.
/config.yaml
/config.*.yaml
*.token
*.credentials.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------- 2. BUSINESS DATA
# eBay listings ledger — account/inventory activity, one row per listing with
# our ask. Kept locally.
listings_log.txt
listings_ledger.csv

# Sales ledger — what each item ACTUALLY sold for, plus eBay's fee and our net.
# Written by lib/sync_actuals.py from the Fulfillment API. This is revenue data;
# it is the single most sensitive file the pipeline produces.
sales_ledger.csv

# Any dated backup of the above (e.g. listings_ledger.backup-20260815.csv).
*.backup-*.csv
*_ledger.backup*.csv

# Performance reports — REPORT-phase output. Gross, fees, net, per-category
# medians and item-level sale prices. Regenerate with:
#   python lib/report.py --performance
# The *findings* that matter long-term get encoded into prompts/ instead, which
# is what makes the reports themselves disposable.
/docs/performance-*.md

# Dashboard output — reports/sales_dashboard.html carries gross, fees, net and
# item-level sale prices; reports/ebay_ads.json carries the account's campaigns;
# reports/price_vs_actual.csv carries every ask and what it realised. All class 2.
# Regenerate the whole directory with:
#   python tools/sales_report.py
/reports/

# Inventory working files — private business data + images (photos, per-item
# phase output, comps, SKUs). The default content store; never tracked.
/inventory/

# Photos staged for sharing/consignment outside the pipeline.
/share-inventory/

# Sensitive business documents + correspondence — kept locally, not tracked.
*.docx
letters/

# Entity formation docs — contain PII (legal name, home address). Local only.
/formation/

# ------------------------------------------------------- 3. HEAVY / GENERATED
# Per-run phase output. These normally live under /inventory/ (already excluded
# above), but a shoot directory can be pointed anywhere, so exclude the
# artifacts by name too — they are regenerated on every run and are never source.
NEEDS_REVIEW.md
SOLD.md
comps.csv
comps_board.html
crop_review.jpg
no-exif/
cropped/
.orig/
.orig-rot/

# Apify raw evidence dumps + saved run results (kept locally; not for repo).
apify_run*.json
apify_run*.stderr.txt
apify_runs/

# Local scratch + generated similarity indexes (large/binary, regenerable).
.scratch/
/kb/index/

# Shoot images — heavy binaries, kept on disk only.
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
*.gif
*.heic
*.webp
*.tiff
*.cxf

# ...except small, intentional test fixtures (regression assets must be tracked).
!tests/fixtures/**

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Historical business working data that predates the /inventory/ convention.
# Removed from tracking 2026-08-15: real listing drafts, prices, eBay draft ids,
# and the seller ZIP. Kept on disk; not for a public repo.
/deprecated/PRL-batches/
/deprecated/v1/draft_listings.md

# PREP batch working files — the queue, its log, and the candidate scan. Derived
# from the ledgers plus the shoots themselves, regenerated by re-running the
# scan, and they name live SKUs. Nothing here is worth versioning.
/.prep_batch.json
/.prep_queue.txt
/.prep_check.log
/.prep_apply.log

# ------------------------------------------ 2./3. LOCAL WORKING FILES AT ROOT
# Everything below is written at the repo root by a tool in tools/ and is
# either regenerable or business data. None of it was ignored before, so a
# `git add -A` would have staged inventory_sheet.csv — one row per live listing,
# with our ask — into a PUBLIC repo. That is the reason these rules exist.

# Per-run stdout, audit dumps and hand-built queues. One batch's working set;
# re-run the tool to get them back.
/.*.log
/.*.json
/.*.txt

# Contact sheets, comps boards and review pages rendered to the repo root by
# tools/prep_sheet_html.py, compare_live.py and friends. Rebuild from the
# generator; never edit one by hand.
/*.html

# Inventory views built from the eBay APIs — SKUs, titles and our asking price
# for every live listing. BUSINESS DATA, and regenerable:
#   python tools/ebay_sheet.py       python tools/inventory_sync.py
/inventory_sheet.csv
/inventory_sheet.json
/.inventory_live.json
/.live_listings_consolidated.json

# Resume state + the report for the retroactive photo re-touch. Names live
# listing ids and what was pushed to each.
/_retouch_tracker.json
/updated_listings.md

# Scratch downloads for the tone/saturation audits: listing images pulled back
# from eBay's CDN plus one-off analysis scripts. 380 MB, all re-downloadable —
# what mattered is written into prompts/prep.md, not kept here.
/.tonecheck/
/.comps/

# Raw seller style samples: another seller's live titles and description HTML,
# pulled for measurement. The measured study (_studies/*.md) and the guide are
# committed; the verbatim sample stays local so it can never be mistaken for
# listing input. Re-derive with `python lib/seller_style.py sample <seller>`.
/styleguides/_studies/*.json

# local working backups (ledger/sales/config) — never committed
backups/
session_friction.json
